"""mlxcli v5 — a minimal local agent CLI for oMLX.

Stdlib only (markitdown used via subprocess if installed, for docx/pdf paste).
Low-overhead design: streaming output, bounded history, shared dialogue
defaults, and approval-gated tools with diff preview.

Usage:
  mlxcli [model] [-p "custom system prompt"]
                             Tool calls are pre-approved by default (run_command,
                             write_file, python_interpreter, ssh_read/write/run) —
                             nothing prompts for the rest of the session, and every
                             tool call runs sandboxed inside an Apple `container`
                             instance (see ensure_sandbox_container) instead of
                             directly on the host. Works in both the interactive
                             REPL and headless --run. -y/--yes is still accepted
                             for old scripts/muscle memory but is now a no-op.
  mlxcli [model] --ask       opt back into the old behavior: prompt for approval
                             (with diff preview) before every tool call, and run
                             tool calls directly on the host, unsandboxed — no
                             human-review gate means no need for a sandbox, and
                             vice versa; the two are tied together deliberately.
  mlxcli --run "task"        headless one-shot mode: run a single task, print the
                             result, and exit (no REPL).
  mlxcli --run "task" --verify "shell command"
                             after the model claims completion, run this command as
                             a correctness check (cwd: the default directory). Exit
                             code 0 = pass. On failure, its output is fed back to the
                             model as a new turn (up to 3 attempts) instead of trusting
                             the model's own claim of success.
  mlxcli --run "task" --verify "..." --verify-history DIR
                             also require every .sh/.py script already in DIR to pass
                             (a regression suite accumulated from earlier steps of the
                             same project) — a fix that breaks something two steps back
                             gets caught here. On a full pass, if --verify was a plain
                             "runner script" form (e.g. "bash check.sh"), that script is
                             archived into DIR so it joins the suite for the next step.

Commands:
  /paste <file>  /review <file-or-folder> [glob]  /read <file>  /find <path> <pattern>  /ls <path>  /gitstatus [path]  /gitdiff [path]
  /convert  /model  /models  /resources  /mem  /tokens  /save [file]  /export [file]  /copy  /modelsettings  /errorlog [n]  /defaultdir [path]  /rag [command]  /clear  /help  /exit
"""
